-- title:
--   Membership in the node-local ring over a number field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$ (hypothesis `hker`). Let $a \in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2}=a$ and lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no point $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ other than $0$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $1 \cdot q$ inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume that $f$, as a Laurent series, lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the modular ring of level $1 \cdot q$ over $A$ at the kernel of $\mathrm{red}$, that its image under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of the Laurent series over $k$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, and that this image is nonzero; assume the same three conditions for the image of $f$ under the Fricke involution `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)`. Assume further (hypothesis `hford`) that for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is centred at $(a, a^q)$ — meaning there are $x, y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = a$, $\mathrm{red}\,y = a^q$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}$ positive on both $j - x$ and $j_q - y$, where $j$ is the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb` and $j_q$ that of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq` — one has $W.\mathrm{ord}\, f = 0$. Finally let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $a$ is the image under `redRestrict red K` of some element of `coeffSubring A K` $= A \cap K$, and suppose $f$ lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K`, the subfield of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $K$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$. Then $f$ lies in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) (coeffSubring A K) (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`, that is, there are $r, s \in \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,(A \cap K)$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a, a^q)$ under `pointEval` and $f \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}\,s = \mathrm{modularEval}\,r$.
--
--   This identifies the local ring at a supersingular point of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(q)$ in characteristic $q$ with coefficients in $A \cap K$ as containing every $K$-rational modular function that is regular at the centred places: the function is integral over that local ring and the local ring is integrally closed. It is used in the descent of functions on the node to a number field, being cited in the passage from membership in `modularLocalized` to membership at the point and in the non-vanishing statement for the Frobenius node pair.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_mem_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_isIntegral_of_mem_fieldOver.lean

